  Skeleton for a new tool's reference file in skills/desktop-tools/references/.

  Copy to references/<toolkey>.md and fill every section. Delete this comment.

  Before writing, confirm the tool satisfies the four-point contract in
  references/tool-registry.md, because a tool that meets it needs no
  special-casing anywhere in scripts/tools/toolctl.sh:

    1. A PID lockfile under its own ~/.<name>/ directory, with stale-lock takeover.
    2. --status printing the one-line key=value grammar, exit 0 either way.
    3. --stop returning 0 when it stopped something and 1 when nothing ran,
       clearing the lockfile after confirming the process is gone.
    4. Flat imports tolerating a cd-to-script-dir launch.

  Keep every section. The "Honest limits" section is not optional: both existing
  references carry one, and a reference that only lists capabilities makes Claude
  claim things the tool cannot do.
-->

